      },
      "why": "The pipeline as it is: an app's layout callback returns a Dom, the cascade makes a StyledDom, solver3::layout_document turns it into boxes and a display list, WebRender draws that, a shell per platform shows the result.\nThe weak spot is the solver's state: the display-list switches and counters are process-wide (the patching switch and the moved-run policy are atomics with a per-thread twin for tests, the counters of the patched builds are thread-locals), so a test that flips one leaves every other test of its binary with it.",
