      },
      "why": "The solver's state has an owner now: its switches, memos and counters belong to the window, the cache or the pass, not to the process (2013be9136). The window writes the display-list options into the cache before each pass and layout_document reads them from there; since 6ffdbddfd2 the switches come from the settings and no longer from the environment.\nThe boxes are the same; what moved is where the layout's state lives, which is why the cache has a cutout of its own and the window an arrow to it. Of the five references that were there, two point at code that changed (the fields of Dom and the parameters of layout_document); the other three are the same lines at the new revision.",
